        "inspected": true,
        "observations": "Complete ordinary exterior picture inspected: broken tiered sandstone prangs, central rectangular open portal with orange/pink jambs, low moulded gallery walls, deep dark windows, surviving/collapsed corbel roof sections and raised stone thresholds. No intact full spires or pristine restoration claimed."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Angkor_temples.JPG",
        "author": "Colocho",
        "date": "2006-07-16",
        "license": "CC BY-SA2.5; viewed only",
        "inspected": true,
        "observations": "Complete east outer entrance photo inspected: open deep portal, stepped plinths, moulded sandstone jambs, corbelled side wings with ridge ornaments, central upper face block with rounded cheeks/nose/smile, multiple diminishing stone crown tiers and foliage outside the structure. The mapped outer east gate is about350m from the central group; do not put this face tower on an inner gate."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banteay_Kdei_05.jpg",
        "author": "Stefan Fussan",
        "date": "2007-12-06",
        "license": "CC BY-SA3.0 and other listed versions; viewed only",
        "inspected": true,
        "observations": "Complete ordinary inner view inspected: several tiered ruined towers, intact narrow corbelled/barrel-like gallery roof, closed moulded wall bands, real dark rectangular window recesses with stone frames, and broken open lintel/pillar sections. Exact roof-survival pattern, fine apsara carving and individual rubble placement remain simplified."
      }
    ]
